---
source: tests/golden_reports.rs
expression: "render(&SarifReporter::new())"
---
{
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v[VERSION]/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "[VERSION]",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "sbom-tools",
          "version": "[VERSION]",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/sbom-tool/sbom-tools",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-001",
              "name": "ComponentAdded",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A new component was added to the SBOM"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A component of the new SBOM has no match in the old SBOM."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Confirm that the added component is an intended dependency, and review its license, supplier and known vulnerabilities before release.",
                "markdown": "Confirm that the added component is an intended dependency, and review its license, supplier and known vulnerabilities before release."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-002",
              "name": "ComponentRemoved",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A component was removed from the SBOM"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A component of the old SBOM has no match in the new SBOM."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Confirm that the component was removed on purpose. An unexpected removal can mean that the SBOM generator missed part of the build.",
                "markdown": "Confirm that the component was removed on purpose. An unexpected removal can mean that the SBOM generator missed part of the build."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-003",
              "name": "VersionChanged",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A component version was changed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A component matched across the two SBOMs changed its version or another field."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Review the change: read the component's release notes, and check the new version's license and known vulnerabilities.",
                "markdown": "Review the change: read the component's release notes, and check the new version's license and known vulnerabilities."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-004",
              "name": "LicenseChanged",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A license was added or changed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A license expression that no component of the old SBOM declared appears in the new SBOM."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Check the new license against the project's license policy (sbom-tools license-check) before release.",
                "markdown": "Check the new license against the project's license policy (sbom-tools license-check) before release."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-005",
              "name": "VulnerabilityIntroduced",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A new vulnerability was introduced"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability affects a component of the new SBOM that it did not affect in the old SBOM."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Upgrade or patch the affected component, or record in a VEX statement why the vulnerability does not affect the product.",
                "markdown": "Upgrade or patch the affected component, or record in a VEX statement why the vulnerability does not affect the product."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-006",
              "name": "VulnerabilityResolved",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was resolved"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability that affected a component of the old SBOM no longer affects the new SBOM."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "No action is needed: the result records the fix.",
                "markdown": "No action is needed: the result records the fix."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-007",
              "name": "SupplierChanged",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A component supplier was changed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A component matched across the two SBOMs names a different supplier."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Confirm that the new supplier is expected: a supplier change can signal a fork, a change of maintainer or a substituted package.",
                "markdown": "Confirm that the new supplier is expected: a supplier change can signal a fork, a change of maintainer or a substituted package."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-TOOLS-008",
              "name": "MetadataChanged",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A document-level metadata field was changed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A document-level field (name, spec version, creation time, creator tool, lifecycle phase, signature, ...) differs between the two SBOMs."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Confirm that the change is expected, for example a regenerated SBOM or an upgraded generator.",
                "markdown": "Confirm that the change is expected, for example a regenerated SBOM or an upgraded generator."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EOL-001",
              "name": "ComponentEndOfLife",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A component has reached end-of-life"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "End-of-life data marks the component's version as no longer supported."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Upgrade to a supported release or replace the component: an end-of-life version receives no security updates.",
                "markdown": "Upgrade to a supported release or replace the component: an end-of-life version receives no security updates."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-EOL-002",
              "name": "ComponentApproachingEol",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A component is approaching end-of-life"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "End-of-life data shows the component's version reaching end-of-life soon."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Plan the upgrade to a supported release before the end-of-life date.",
                "markdown": "Plan the upgrade to a supported release before the end-of-life date."
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SBOM-FRESHNESS",
              "name": "CraSbomFreshness",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(7) / Annex I Part II (1): SBOM freshness — timely regeneration after changes"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(7) / Annex I Part II (1): SBOM freshness — timely regeneration after changes. References: CRA Art. 13(7); CRA Annex I Part II (1); ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Regenerate the SBOM when components are added, removed, or updated. CRA Art. 13(7) requires manufacturers to systematically document relevant cybersecurity aspects, and the Annex I Part II (1) SBOM must reflect the product's current components. A creation timestamp later than the evaluation date is reported like a missing one: correct the generator's clock or time zone.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Regenerate the SBOM when components are added, removed, or updated. CRA Art. 13(7) requires manufacturers to systematically document relevant cybersecurity aspects, and the Annex I Part II (1) SBOM must reflect the product's current components. A creation timestamp later than the evaluation date is reported like a missing one: correct the generator's clock or time zone.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-MACHINE-READABLE",
              "name": "CraMachineReadableFormat",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM must be in a commonly used, machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.3+, or SPDX 3.0+)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM must be in a commonly used, machine-readable format (CycloneDX 1.4+, SPDX 2.3+, or SPDX 3.0+). References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-04; ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Ensure the SBOM is produced in CycloneDX 1.4+ (JSON or XML), SPDX 2.3+ (JSON or tag-value), or SPDX 3.0+ (JSON-LD). Older format versions may not be recognized as machine-readable under CRA Annex I Part II (1).\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-04\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.2 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Ensure the SBOM is produced in CycloneDX 1.4+ (JSON or XML), SPDX 2.3+ (JSON or tag-value), or SPDX 3.0+ (JSON-LD). Older format versions may not be recognized as machine-readable under CRA Annex I Part II (1).\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-04\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.2](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-17-CONTACT",
              "name": "CraVulnerabilityContact",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(17): Single point of contact for vulnerability reporting (Annex I Part II (6), Annex II (2))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(17): Single point of contact for vulnerability reporting (Annex I Part II (6), Annex II (2)). References: CRA Art. 13(17); CRA Annex I Part II (6); CRA Annex II (2)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give the product a single point of contact for vulnerability reports (Art. 13(17)): a security contact or vulnerability-disclosure URL referenced from the product component. securityContact or vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl in the CRA sidecar lowers the finding to Info. A contact must reach someone: placeholders such as NOASSERTION, unknown, n/a or TBD, and addresses at example.com, example.net or example.org, do not count.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(17) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex I Part II (6) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (2) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give the product a single point of contact for vulnerability reports (Art. 13(17)): a security contact or vulnerability-disclosure URL referenced from the product component. securityContact or vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl in the CRA sidecar lowers the finding to Info. A contact must reach someone: placeholders such as NOASSERTION, unknown, n/a or TBD, and addresses at example.com, example.net or example.org, do not count.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type security-contact (or advisories).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory to the root package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(17)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (6)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (2)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-METADATA",
              "name": "CraVulnerabilityMetadata",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability entries carry a severity or CVSS score"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability entries carry a severity or CVSS score. References: CRA Annex I Part II (4)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every vulnerability entry a severity or CVSS score (Annex I Part II (4)). An entry whose VEX statement is not_affected and names a justification needs neither: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set vulnerabilities[].ratings[] on each entry with a severity (critical, high, medium, low) or a CVSS score.\n- SPDX 2.x: documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a security_CvssV3VulnAssessmentRelationship (security_score, security_vectorString) for each vulnerability.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (4) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give every vulnerability entry a severity or CVSS score (Annex I Part II (4)). An entry whose VEX statement is not\\_affected and names a justification needs neither: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set vulnerabilities\\[\\].ratings\\[\\] on each entry with a severity (critical, high, medium, low) or a CVSS score.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, so these entries were attached by enrichment.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a security\\_CvssV3VulnAssessmentRelationship (security\\_score, security\\_vectorString) for each vulnerability.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (4)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-METADATA-REMEDIATION",
              "name": "CraVulnerabilityRemediationDetail",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability remediations name a fixed version or describe the fix"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): Vulnerability remediations name a fixed version or describe the fix. References: CRA Annex I Part II (4)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every vulnerability remediation a fixed version or a description of the fix (Annex I Part II (4)). A vulnerability whose VEX statement is not_affected and names a justification is exempt: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: an entry whose analysis.response declares update or workaround_available needs the details: set vulnerabilities[].recommendation to the fix (a fixed version or the steps to take), or vulnerabilities[].workaround to the workaround.\n- SPDX 2.x: documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 2.x input.\n- SPDX 3.0: the parser builds no remediation from this format, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 3.0 input.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (4) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give every vulnerability remediation a fixed version or a description of the fix (Annex I Part II (4)). A vulnerability whose VEX statement is not\\_affected and names a justification is exempt: it documents a vulnerability that cannot be exploited in the product, which the CRA FAQ (v1.4, 4.3.1) says the manufacturer may decide not to fix.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** an entry whose analysis.response declares update or workaround\\_available needs the details: set vulnerabilities\\[\\].recommendation to the fix (a fixed version or the steps to take), or vulnerabilities\\[\\].workaround to the workaround.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** documents in this format carry no vulnerability data, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 2.x input.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** the parser builds no remediation from this format, and enrichment records a fixed version with every remediation it adds, so the check does not fire on SPDX 3.0 input.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (4)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-METADATA-PROFILE",
              "name": "CraSecurityProfileConformance",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): SPDX 3.0 Security profile declared for a document that carries vulnerabilities"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (4): SPDX 3.0 Security profile declared for a document that carries vulnerabilities. References: CRA Annex I Part II (4)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare SPDX 3.0 Security profile conformance when the document carries vulnerabilities, so the vulnerability information it conveys is complete (Annex I Part II (4)).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- SPDX 2.x: the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- SPDX 3.0: list security in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (4) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare SPDX 3.0 Security profile conformance when the document carries vulnerabilities, so the vulnerability information it conveys is complete (Annex I Part II (4)).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** list security in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (4)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-5",
              "name": "CraLicensedComponentTracking",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): Third-party due diligence — license information for all components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): Third-party due diligence — license information for all components. References: CRA Art. 13(5); ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Record license information for every component to support the Art. 13(5) due diligence on integrated third-party components.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].licenses[] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages[].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing_LicenseExpression element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(5) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Record license information for every component to support the Art. 13(5) due diligence on integrated third-party components.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].licenses\\[\\] entries (license.id with an SPDX identifier, or an expression).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].licenseDeclared (PackageLicenseDeclared) or packages\\[\\].licenseConcluded; NOASSERTION and NONE are read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a hasDeclaredLicense (or hasConcludedLicense) Relationship from the package to a simplelicensing\\_LicenseExpression element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(5)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-5-PROFILE",
              "name": "CraLicensingProfileConformance",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile declared for a document that carries license data"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(5): SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile declared for a document that carries license data. References: CRA Art. 13(5)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile conformance when the document carries license data, so its Art. 13(5) licence evidence is conveyed completely.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- SPDX 2.x: the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- SPDX 3.0: list simpleLicensing in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(5) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare SPDX 3.0 SimpleLicensing profile conformance when the document carries license data, so its Art. 13(5) licence evidence is conveyed completely.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** the check does not run on CycloneDX input.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** the check does not run on SPDX 2.x input.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** list simpleLicensing in the SpdxDocument's profileConformance.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(5)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-CVD-POLICY",
              "name": "CraCoordinatedDisclosure",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (5): Coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy reference"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (5): Coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy reference. References: CRA Annex I Part II (5); CRA Art. 13(8); prEN 40000-1-3: RLS-2-RQ-03-RE."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy (Annex I Part II (5)) from the product component. In the CRA sidecar, coordinatedDisclosurePolicyUrl satisfies the open-source steward profile and vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl lowers the manufacturer finding to Info. A placeholder URL or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type advisories linking the policy.\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) linking the policy to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory linking the policy to the root package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (5) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: RLS-2-RQ-03-RE",
                "markdown": "Reference the coordinated vulnerability disclosure policy (Annex I Part II (5)) from the product component. In the CRA sidecar, coordinatedDisclosurePolicyUrl satisfies the open-source steward profile and vulnerabilityDisclosureUrl lowers the manufacturer finding to Info. A placeholder URL or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type advisories linking the policy.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory SECURITY and referenceType advisory (or url) linking the policy to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType securityAdvisory linking the policy to the root package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (5)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: RLS-2-RQ-03-RE"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-8",
              "name": "CraSupportPeriod",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / 13(19): Support period and security update end date (Annex II (7))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / 13(19): Support period and security update end date (Annex II (7)). References: CRA Art. 13(8); CRA Art. 13(19); CRA Annex II (7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare when security updates end (Art. 13(8) / 13(19)): set supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar, or record the date in the SBOM.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.properties[] entry named end-of-support whose value is the date (RFC 3339 or YYYY-MM-DD).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- SPDX 3.0: validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 13(19) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare when security updates end (Art. 13(8) / 13(19)): set supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar, or record the date in the SBOM.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.properties\\[\\] entry named end-of-support whose value is the date (RFC 3339 or YYYY-MM-DD).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 13(19)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-8-EOL",
              "name": "CraEndOfLifeComponents",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8): Components past end-of-life, which receive no more security updates"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8): Components past end-of-life, which receive no more security updates. References: CRA Art. 13(8)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Upgrade or replace the components the end-of-life data marks as no longer supported: they receive no more security updates (Art. 13(8)).\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Upgrade or replace the components the end-of-life data marks as no longer supported: they receive no more security updates (Art. 13(8)).\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-LIFECYCLE",
              "name": "CraComponentLifecycle",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Component lifecycle and end-of-support status"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Component lifecycle and end-of-support status. References: CRA Art. 13(8); CRA Annex II (7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Record component lifecycle or end-of-support status (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)); supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar counts too.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add an eol, lifecycle or end-of-support entry to components[].properties[] (or an end-of-support date to metadata.component.properties[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- SPDX 3.0: validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Record component lifecycle or end-of-support status (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)); supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar counts too.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add an eol, lifecycle or end-of-support entry to components\\[\\].properties\\[\\] (or an end-of-support date to metadata.component.properties\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].validUntilDate (ValidUntilDate) on the described package as an RFC 3339 date-time.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** validUntilTime and supportLevel are not read, so use supportEndDate in the CRA sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-LIFECYCLE-APPROACHING-EOL",
              "name": "CraApproachingEndOfLife",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Components reaching end-of-life within six months"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7): Components reaching end-of-life within six months. References: CRA Art. 13(8); CRA Annex II (7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Plan replacements for the components the end-of-life data shows reaching end-of-life within six months (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)).\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(8) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Plan replacements for the components the end-of-life data shows reaching end-of-life within six months (Art. 13(8) / Annex II (7)).\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(8)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-15-PRODUCT",
              "name": "CraProductIdentification",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(15): Product identification (Annex II (3))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(15): Product identification (Annex II (3)). References: CRA Art. 13(15); CRA Annex II (3)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name the product the SBOM describes (Art. 13(15)); productName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info, but the SBOM should carry the name itself.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component.name.\n- SPDX 2.x: set the document name (DocumentName).\n- SPDX 3.0: set name on the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(15) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (3) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Name the product the SBOM describes (Art. 13(15)); productName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info, but the SBOM should carry the name itself.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component.name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set the document name (DocumentName).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set name on the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(15)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (3)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-COMPONENT-VERSION",
              "name": "CraComponentVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component version identification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component version identification. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-06; ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Every component must have a version string. Use the actual release version (e.g., '1.2.3'), not a range or placeholder.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-06\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Every component must have a version string. Use the actual release version (e.g., '1.2.3'), not a range or placeholder.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-06\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-16",
              "name": "CraManufacturerIdentification",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Manufacturer identification and contact information (Annex II (1))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Manufacturer identification and contact information (Annex II (1)). References: CRA Art. 13(16); CRA Annex II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the manufacturer (Art. 13(16)): as the manufacturer or supplier of the product component, or as an organization creator of the SBOM; placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count. manufacturerName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component.manufacturer (CycloneDX 1.6+) or metadata.supplier, or metadata.manufacturer for the organization that created the SBOM (name, contact[].email).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier on the described package, e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or add a creationInfo.creators[] entry \"Organization: Example Ltd (contact@example.com)\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the root package to an Organization element, or set creationInfo.createdBy to one.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(16) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Identify the manufacturer (Art. 13(16)): as the manufacturer or supplier of the product component, or as an organization creator of the SBOM; placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count. manufacturerName in the CRA sidecar lowers this to Info.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component.manufacturer (CycloneDX 1.6+) or metadata.supplier, or metadata.manufacturer for the organization that created the SBOM (name, contact\\[\\].email).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier on the described package, e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or add a creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry \"Organization: Example Ltd (contact@example.com)\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the root package to an Organization element, or set creationInfo.createdBy to one.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(16)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-16-EMAIL",
              "name": "CraManufacturerEmail",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Valid manufacturer contact email (Annex II (1))"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(16): Valid manufacturer contact email (Annex II (1)). References: CRA Art. 13(16); CRA Annex II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Provide a valid contact email for the manufacturer. The email must contain an @ sign with valid local and domain parts.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: correct the metadata.manufacturer.contact[].email address.\n- SPDX 2.x: correct the address in the \"Organization: Name (email)\" creationInfo.creators[] entry.\n- SPDX 3.0: agent emails are not read from SPDX 3.0 documents, so this check does not apply.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(16) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Annex II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Provide a valid contact email for the manufacturer. The email must contain an @ sign with valid local and domain parts.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** correct the metadata.manufacturer.contact\\[\\].email address.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** correct the address in the \"Organization: Name (email)\" creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entry.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** agent emails are not read from SPDX 3.0 documents, so this check does not apply.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(16)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Annex II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-COMPONENT-SUPPLIER",
              "name": "CraComponentSupplier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component supplier identification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Component supplier identification. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03; ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify each component's supplier; placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Identify each component's supplier; placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-VULN-STATEMENT",
              "name": "CraKnownVulnerabilities",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Documented vulnerability information — vulnerability data or assertion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Documented vulnerability information — vulnerability data or assertion. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Include the product's known vulnerabilities in the SBOM, or reference the vulnerability disclosure report (VDR) or VEX that states them (Annex I Part II (1)).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: list them in vulnerabilities[] with affects[].ref pointing at the affected components, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalReferences[] entry of type vulnerability-assertion or exploitability-statement.\n- SPDX 2.x: no field carries vulnerability data, and no external reference category names a VDR or VEX.\n- SPDX 3.0: add security_Vulnerability elements linked to the affected packages by affects Relationships, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType vulnerabilityDisclosureReport or vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Include the product's known vulnerabilities in the SBOM, or reference the vulnerability disclosure report (VDR) or VEX that states them (Annex I Part II (1)).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** list them in vulnerabilities\\[\\] with affects\\[\\].ref pointing at the affected components, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type vulnerability-assertion or exploitability-statement.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no field carries vulnerability data, and no external reference category names a VDR or VEX.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add security\\_Vulnerability elements linked to the affected packages by affects Relationships, or reference the published VDR or VEX from an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType vulnerabilityDisclosureReport or vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-IDENTIFIER",
              "name": "CraComponentIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Unique identifier (PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID) on every component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Unique identifier (PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID) on every component. References: CRA Annex I; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07; ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1; ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID to each component for unique identification. PURLs are preferred (e.g., pkg:npm/lodash@4.17.21).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].purl (or cpe, or swhid[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier[] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Add a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID to each component for unique identification. PURLs are preferred (e.g., pkg:npm/lodash@4.17.21).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].purl (or cpe, or swhid\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-TRACEABILITY",
              "name": "CraPrimaryTraceability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Primary product component traceable across updates by a PURL or CPE"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Primary product component traceable across updates by a PURL or CPE. References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07; ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give the primary product component a PURL or CPE so it can be traced across updates (Annex I Part II (1)); a SWHID or SWID alone does not satisfy this check.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component.purl (or cpe).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a PACKAGE-MANAGER purl or SECURITY cpe23Type packages[].externalRefs[] entry to the described package.\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl on the rootElement package, or add a cpe23 externalIdentifier[] entry to it.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Give the primary product component a PURL or CPE so it can be traced across updates (Annex I Part II (1)); a SWHID or SWID alone does not satisfy this check.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component.purl (or cpe).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a PACKAGE-MANAGER purl or SECURITY cpe23Type packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry to the described package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl on the rootElement package, or add a cpe23 externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry to it.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §3.2](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-SUPPLY-CHAIN",
              "name": "CraDirectDependencySupplier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Supplier of every direct dependency identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, mandatory)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Supplier of every direct dependency identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, mandatory). References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03; ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the supplier of every direct dependency, one hop from the primary component or, when none is declared, from a root of the dependency graph (mandatory under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Identify the supplier of every direct dependency, one hop from the primary component or, when none is declared, from a root of the dependency graph (mandatory under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-SUPPLY-CHAIN-TRANSITIVE",
              "name": "CraTransitiveDependencySupplier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Suppliers of transitive dependencies identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, recommended)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II: Suppliers of transitive dependencies identified (PRE-7-RQ-03, recommended). References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03; ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the suppliers of transitive dependencies as well (recommended under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Identify the suppliers of transitive dependencies as well (recommended under PRE-7-RQ-03).\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-01\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-03\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-INTEGRITY",
              "name": "CraComponentHash",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Component hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) for integrity verification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Component hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) for integrity verification. References: CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f); ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].hashes[] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- SPDX 2.x: add packages[].checksums[] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- SPDX 3.0: add verifiedUsing[] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-DEPENDENCY",
              "name": "CraDependencyRelationships",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Dependency relationships connect the primary component to its dependencies"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Dependency relationships connect the primary component to its dependencies. References: CRA Annex I; ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add dependency relationships between components: connect the primary component to its direct dependencies and keep most components inside the dependency graph.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add dependencies[] entries (ref plus dependsOn[]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- SPDX 2.x: add relationships[] entries such as DEPENDS_ON (or DEPENDENCY_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- SPDX 3.0: add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Add dependency relationships between components: connect the primary component to its direct dependencies and keep most components inside the dependency graph.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add dependencies\\[\\] entries (ref plus dependsOn\\[\\]); an entry with an empty dependsOn records a component that has no dependencies.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add relationships\\[\\] entries such as DEPENDS\\_ON (or DEPENDENCY\\_OF, CONTAINS) between the packages.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add Relationship elements with relationshipType dependsOn (or contains) between the packages.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-DEPENDENCY-ROOTS",
              "name": "CraAmbiguousDependencyRoots",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Primary component identified when the dependency graph has several roots"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Primary component identified when the dependency graph has several roots. References: CRA Annex I."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the primary product component when the dependency graph has several roots, so the product's top-level dependencies are unambiguous.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- SPDX 2.x: name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- SPDX 3.0: set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Identify the primary product component when the dependency graph has several roots, so the product's top-level dependencies are unambiguous.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-CYCLES",
              "name": "CraDependencyCycles",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Dependency graph must be an acyclic inventory — cyclic dependency declarations detected"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): Dependency graph must be an acyclic inventory — cyclic dependency declarations detected. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Resolve cyclic dependency declarations so the SBOM's dependency graph is a directed acyclic inventory of the product's components.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Resolve cyclic dependency declarations so the SBOM's dependency graph is a directed acyclic inventory of the product's components.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-PRIMARY",
              "name": "CraPrimaryComponent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Top-level product component identified"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I: Top-level product component identified. References: CRA Annex I."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify the top-level product component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- SPDX 2.x: name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- SPDX 3.0: set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Identify the top-level product component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component to the product's component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** name the product package in documentDescribes (or add a DESCRIBES relationship from SPDXRef-DOCUMENT).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set rootElement on the SpdxDocument to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-I-CONTROLS",
              "name": "CraAnnexIControlEvidence",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I: Evidence URL for every control the CRA sidecar marks satisfied"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I: Evidence URL for every control the CRA sidecar marks satisfied. References: CRA Annex I."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every control the CRA sidecar's annexIPartIControls block marks satisfied an evidenceUrl pointing at its evidence (test report, design review, scan output), or set satisfied to false until the evidence exists.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give every control the CRA sidecar's annexIPartIControls block marks satisfied an evidenceUrl pointing at its evidence (test report, design review, scan output), or set satisfied to false until the evidence exists.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-INVENTORY",
              "name": "CraInventory",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM inventories the product's software components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part II (1): SBOM inventories the product's software components. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set metadata.component and list the components in components[].\n- SPDX 2.x: list the packages in packages[] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- SPDX 3.0: add software_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "List the software components the product is made of. A document with no components, or with only files, snippets or cryptographic assets, is not a software inventory; validate a CBOM with --standard cnsa2 or pqc instead.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set metadata.component and list the components in components\\[\\].\n- **SPDX 2.x:** list the packages in packages\\[\\] and name the product in documentDescribes.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add software\\_Package elements and set the SpdxDocument's rootElement to the product package.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-DOC-INTEGRITY",
              "name": "CraDocumentIntegrity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Document integrity — a digital signature, or an attestation carrying a hash"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f): Document integrity — a digital signature, or an attestation carrying a hash. References: CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f); ENISA SBOM TA: §2.2.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Protect the SBOM's integrity (Annex I Part I (2)(f)): sign the document, or reference from the product component an attestation or certification that carries the hash of the referenced document. A serial number identifies the document but does not protect its integrity.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: sign the BOM (a JSF signature object at the document root in JSON, an enveloped XML-DSig <Signature> element on <bom> in XML), or add hashes[] to a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type attestation or certification-report.\n- SPDX 2.x: no in-document signature field exists and external references carry no hash, so the check cannot be satisfied from the document.\n- SPDX 3.0: add a verifiedUsing[] entry of type signature (algorithm, hashValue) to the SpdxDocument.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.2.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Protect the SBOM's integrity (Annex I Part I (2)(f)): sign the document, or reference from the product component an attestation or certification that carries the hash of the referenced document. A serial number identifies the document but does not protect its integrity.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** sign the BOM (a JSF signature object at the document root in JSON, an enveloped XML-DSig \\<Signature\\> element on \\<bom\\> in XML), or add hashes\\[\\] to a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type attestation or certification-report.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no in-document signature field exists and external references carry no hash, so the check cannot be satisfied from the document.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add a verifiedUsing\\[\\] entry of type signature (algorithm, hashValue) to the SpdxDocument.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part I (2)(f)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.2.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-V",
              "name": "CraDeclarationOfConformity",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex V: EU Declaration of Conformity reference"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex V: EU Declaration of Conformity reference. References: CRA Annex V."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the EU Declaration of Conformity (Annex V): set ceMarkingReference in the CRA sidecar to the DoC's URL or document ID.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type attestation or certification-report pointing at the DoC also counts.\n- SPDX 2.x: a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory OTHER and referenceType declaration-of-conformity also counts.\n- SPDX 3.0: no reference type names a Declaration of Conformity, but an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation pointing at the DoC also counts.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex V (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the EU Declaration of Conformity (Annex V): set ceMarkingReference in the CRA sidecar to the DoC's URL or document ID.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type attestation or certification-report pointing at the DoC also counts.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory OTHER and referenceType declaration-of-conformity also counts.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** no reference type names a Declaration of Conformity, but an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation pointing at the DoC also counts.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex V](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-13-2",
              "name": "CraRiskAssessment",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(2): Reference to the documented cybersecurity risk assessment"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 13(2): Reference to the documented cybersecurity risk assessment. References: CRA Art. 13(2)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the documented cybersecurity risk assessment Art. 13(2) requires: set riskAssessmentUrl in the CRA sidecar to its URL or document reference.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type risk-assessment pointing at it also counts.\n- SPDX 2.x: no external reference category names a risk assessment, so use the sidecar key.\n- SPDX 3.0: an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType riskAssessment pointing at it also counts.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 13(2) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the documented cybersecurity risk assessment Art. 13(2) requires: set riskAssessmentUrl in the CRA sidecar to its URL or document reference.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type risk-assessment pointing at it also counts.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no external reference category names a risk assessment, so use the sidecar key.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType riskAssessment pointing at it also counts.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 13(2)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-PSIRT",
              "name": "CraPsirtUrl",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14: Public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14: Public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports. References: CRA Art. 14."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports (Art. 14 reporting readiness): set psirtUrl in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar; a placeholder such as TBD or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14 (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Document the public PSIRT URL that receives external vulnerability reports (Art. 14 reporting readiness): set psirtUrl in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar; a placeholder such as TBD or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-EARLY-WARNING",
              "name": "CraEarlyWarningChannel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a): Channel for the 24-hour early warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a): Channel for the 24-hour early warning. References: CRA Art. 14(2)(a); CRA Art. 14(4)(a)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the channel for the 24-hour early warning of an actively exploited vulnerability or a severe incident (Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a)): set earlyWarningContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar; a placeholder such as TBD or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14(2)(a) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 14(4)(a) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Document the channel for the 24-hour early warning of an actively exploited vulnerability or a severe incident (Art. 14(2)(a) / 14(4)(a)): set earlyWarningContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar; a placeholder such as TBD or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14(2)(a)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 14(4)(a)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-NOTIFICATION",
              "name": "CraNotificationChannel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b): Channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b): Channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications. References: CRA Art. 14(2)(b); CRA Art. 14(4)(b)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Document the channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications (Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b)): set incidentReportContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar; a placeholder such as TBD or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14(2)(b) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- CRA Art. 14(4)(b) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Document the channel for the 72-hour vulnerability and incident notifications (Art. 14(2)(b) / 14(4)(b)): set incidentReportContact in the CRA sidecar. This check reads only the sidecar; a placeholder such as TBD or an address at example.com, example.net or example.org does not count.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14(2)(b)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [CRA Art. 14(4)(b)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ART-14-ENISA",
              "name": "CraEnisaPlatformIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(7): How the manufacturer reaches the ENISA single reporting platform"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Art. 14(7): How the manufacturer reaches the ENISA single reporting platform. References: CRA Art. 14(7)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name the CSIRT designated as coordinator in enisaReportingPlatformId in the CRA sidecar: the one Art. 14(7) assigns by the manufacturer's main establishment and every notification selects on the ENISA Single Reporting Platform (https://portal.cra-srp.enisa.europa.eu/), through which Art. 14(1), (3) and (7) route notifications since 2026-09-11. Naming that CSIRT satisfies this finding. Do not register on the platform early to clear it: no registration is needed before a notification is due, and ENISA advises registering only then. A registration already made may be recorded instead. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Art. 14(7) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Name the CSIRT designated as coordinator in enisaReportingPlatformId in the CRA sidecar: the one Art. 14(7) assigns by the manufacturer's main establishment and every notification selects on the ENISA Single Reporting Platform (https://portal.cra-srp.enisa.europa.eu/), through which Art. 14(1), (3) and (7) route notifications since 2026-09-11. Naming that CSIRT satisfies this finding. Do not register on the platform early to clear it: no registration is needed before a notification is due, and ENISA advises registering only then. A registration already made may be recorded instead. This check reads only the sidecar.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Art. 14(7)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-IV",
              "name": "CraEuccCertification",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex IV: EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex IV: EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires. References: CRA Annex IV."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires: set euccProtectionProfileId, euccTargetOfEvaluation, euccItsefIdentifier or an unexpired euccValidUntil in the CRA sidecar. Once euccValidUntil has passed, the certificate is expired and none of these keys counts. The product classes are CRA Annex III (important, class I and II) and Annex IV (critical); Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392 describes which products each category covers.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: an externalReferences[] entry of type certification-report or attestation whose URL contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted, as is a fresh, fully conformant attestation in declarations (CycloneDX 1.6+) of a CRA standard that names EUCC or Common Criteria.\n- SPDX 2.x: no field is recognized as an EUCC reference, so use the sidecar keys.\n- SPDX 3.0: an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation whose locator contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex IV (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the EUCC (Common Criteria) certification the product class requires: set euccProtectionProfileId, euccTargetOfEvaluation, euccItsefIdentifier or an unexpired euccValidUntil in the CRA sidecar. Once euccValidUntil has passed, the certificate is expired and none of these keys counts. The product classes are CRA Annex III (important, class I and II) and Annex IV (critical); Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392 describes which products each category covers.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** an externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type certification-report or attestation whose URL contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted, as is a fresh, fully conformant attestation in declarations (CycloneDX 1.6+) of a CRA standard that names EUCC or Common Criteria.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no field is recognized as an EUCC reference, so use the sidecar keys.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType certificationReport or secureSoftwareAttestation whose locator contains eucc, common-criteria or commoncriteria is also accepted.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex IV](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ANNEX-VIII",
              "name": "CraConformityAssessment",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex VIII: Conformity-assessment evidence for the resolved assessment route"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA Annex VIII: Conformity-assessment evidence for the resolved assessment route. References: CRA Annex VIII."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reference the notified-body or certification-body certificate the conformity-assessment route requires — the EU-type examination certificate (Module B+C), the quality-system approval (Module H) or the EUCC certificate — as a certification external reference on the product component. An attestation reference does not count here, since it may be a self-attestation; it still serves as the Annex V Declaration of Conformity reference. The route follows the product class (Art. 32; Annex III class I and II, Annex IV critical), whose product categories Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392 describes.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add a metadata.component.externalReferences[] entry of type certification-report; an attestation entry does not count.\n- SPDX 2.x: no external reference category names a certificate, so the check cannot be satisfied from the document.\n- SPDX 3.0: add an externalRef[] entry with externalRefType certificationReport to the root package; secureSoftwareAttestation does not count.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex VIII (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Reference the notified-body or certification-body certificate the conformity-assessment route requires — the EU-type examination certificate (Module B+C), the quality-system approval (Module H) or the EUCC certificate — as a certification external reference on the product component. An attestation reference does not count here, since it may be a self-attestation; it still serves as the Annex V Declaration of Conformity reference. The route follows the product class (Art. 32; Annex III class I and II, Annex IV critical), whose product categories Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392 describes.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add a metadata.component.externalReferences\\[\\] entry of type certification-report; an attestation entry does not count.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** no external reference category names a certificate, so the check cannot be satisfied from the document.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add an externalRef\\[\\] entry with externalRefType certificationReport to the root package; secureSoftwareAttestation does not count.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex VIII](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-CREATOR",
              "name": "CraSbomCreator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM creator identified (person, organization or tool)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM creator identified (person, organization or tool). References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Identify who created the SBOM: a person, organization or tool.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add metadata.authors[] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- SPDX 2.x: add creationInfo.creators[] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Identify who created the SBOM: a person, organization or tool.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add metadata.authors\\[\\] (name, email), metadata.manufacturer or metadata.tools.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add creationInfo.creators\\[\\] entries such as \"Organization: Example Ltd (sbom@example.com)\" or \"Tool: generator-1.0\".\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.createdBy to a Person or Organization element, or createdUsing to a Tool element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SERIAL",
              "name": "CraDocumentIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM carries a unique document identifier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SBOM carries a unique document identifier. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give the SBOM a unique document identifier.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set serialNumber (urn:uuid:…).\n- SPDX 2.x: set documentNamespace (DocumentNamespace) to a unique URI.\n- SPDX 3.0: give the SpdxDocument a unique spdxId.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Give the SBOM a unique document identifier.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set serialNumber (urn:uuid:…).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set documentNamespace (DocumentNamespace) to a unique URI.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** give the SpdxDocument a unique spdxId.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-COMPONENT-NAME",
              "name": "CraComponentName",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every component has a name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every component has a name. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1); ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every component a name; empty names and placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].name.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].name (PackageName), or files[].fileName for files.\n- SPDX 3.0: set name on the element.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1 (https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials)",
                "markdown": "Give every component a name; empty names and placeholders such as NOASSERTION do not count.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].name (PackageName), or files\\[\\].fileName for files.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set name on the element.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- [ENISA SBOM TA: §2.1.1](<https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SPEC-VERSION",
              "name": "CraSpecVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Spec version sbom-tools reads (CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Spec version sbom-tools reads (CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0). References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use a spec version sbom-tools reads: CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0. An older version lacks fields the checks read, and what a newer version adds is not evaluated.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- SPDX 2.x: set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Use a spec version sbom-tools reads: CycloneDX 1.4–1.7, SPDX 2.x or 3.0. An older version lacks fields the checks read, and what a newer version adds is not evaluated.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-SPEC-VERSION-UNKNOWN",
              "name": "CraSpecVersionUnknown",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SPDX document declares a valid SPDX version"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: SPDX document declares a valid SPDX version. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Declare a valid SPDX version, 2.x or 3.0, so the document is read as the version it is.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- SPDX 2.x: set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- SPDX 3.0: set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Declare a valid SPDX version, 2.x or 3.0, so the document is read as the version it is.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set specVersion 1.4–1.7.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set spdxVersion SPDX-2.x.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set creationInfo.specVersion 3.0.x.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-ELEMENT-ID",
              "name": "CraElementIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every element has its own well-formed identifier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every element has its own well-formed identifier. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every element its own well-formed identifier, the one dependency relationships refer to.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set a bom-ref on every component, one that differs from the component's name.\n- SPDX 2.x: give every element an SPDXID that starts with SPDXRef-.\n- SPDX 3.0: give every element an IRI spdxId.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "Give every element its own well-formed identifier, the one dependency relationships refer to.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set a bom-ref on every component, one that differs from the component's name.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** give every element an SPDXID that starts with SPDXRef-.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** give every element an IRI spdxId.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-DUPLICATE-COMPONENT",
              "name": "CraDuplicateComponent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every component is listed once"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA readiness: Every component is listed once. References: CRA Annex I Part II (1)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "List each component once. Entries that share an identifier (purl, CPE, SWHID or SWID, else the element identifier) and a name and version describe one component: sbom-tools merges them, so the verdict does not depend on their order, and names the fields on which they disagree. Fix the generator so that it writes one entry per component.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: list each component once in components[], under a bom-ref of its own.\n- SPDX 2.x: list each package once in packages[], under an SPDXID of its own.\n- SPDX 3.0: describe each package in one software_Package element, under an spdxId of its own.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (1) (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)",
                "markdown": "List each component once. Entries that share an identifier (purl, CPE, SWHID or SWID, else the element identifier) and a name and version describe one component: sbom-tools merges them, so the verdict does not depend on their order, and names the fields on which they disagree. Fix the generator so that it writes one entry per component.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** list each component once in components\\[\\], under a bom-ref of its own.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** list each package once in packages\\[\\], under an SPDXID of its own.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** describe each package in one software\\_Package element, under an spdxId of its own.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II (1)](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-PRODUCER",
              "name": "CraHardwareProducer",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Producer of every hardware component (device, firmware, driver)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Producer of every hardware component (device, firmware, driver). References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Name the producer (supplier or author) of every hardware component: device, firmware or device driver.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors[].name).\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages[].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- SPDX 3.0: set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Name the producer (supplier or author) of every hardware component: device, firmware or device driver.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].supplier.name (or manufacturer.name, or authors\\[\\].name).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].supplier (PackageSupplier), e.g. \"Organization: Example Ltd\", or packages\\[\\].originator (PackageOriginator); a NOASSERTION value is read as absent.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set suppliedBy on the package to the spdxId of an Organization or Person element.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-IDENTIFIER",
              "name": "CraHardwareIdentifier",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Unique identifier on every hardware component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Unique identifier on every hardware component. References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every hardware component a unique identifier: a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].purl (or cpe, or swhid[]).\n- SPDX 2.x: add a packages[].externalRefs[] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier[] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Give every hardware component a unique identifier: a PURL, CPE, SWHID or SWID.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].purl (or cpe, or swhid\\[\\]).\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add a packages\\[\\].externalRefs\\[\\] entry with referenceCategory PACKAGE-MANAGER, referenceType purl and a pkg: locator (or a SECURITY cpe23Type, or a PERSISTENT-ID swh entry).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageUrl, or add an externalIdentifier\\[\\] entry with externalIdentifierType packageUrl, cpe23, swhid or swid.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-FIRMWARE-VERSION",
              "name": "CraFirmwareVersion",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Version of every firmware component"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Version of every firmware component. References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every firmware component its firmware version.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the package.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Give every firmware component its firmware version.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo (PackageVersion).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the package.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-8-RQ-02-DEVICE-FIRMWARE",
              "name": "CraDeviceFirmware",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Every device has a version or a dependency on its firmware"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-8-RQ-02]: Every device has a version or a dependency on its firmware. References: prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every device a version, or a dependency on the firmware component it runs.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: set components[].version on the device, or add a dependencies[] entry from the device to its firmware component.\n- SPDX 2.x: set packages[].versionInfo on the device package, or add a DEPENDS_ON relationships[] entry from it to its firmware package.\n- SPDX 3.0: set software_packageVersion on the device package, or add a dependsOn Relationship from it to its firmware package.\n\nReferences:\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02",
                "markdown": "Give every device a version, or a dependency on the firmware component it runs.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** set components\\[\\].version on the device, or add a dependencies\\[\\] entry from the device to its firmware component.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** set packages\\[\\].versionInfo on the device package, or add a DEPENDS\\_ON relationships\\[\\] entry from it to its firmware package.\n- **SPDX 3.0:** set software\\_packageVersion on the device package, or add a dependsOn Relationship from it to its firmware package.\n\n**References**\n\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-8-RQ-02"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "SBOM-CRA-PRE-7-RQ-07-RE",
              "name": "CraVendorHashCarryThrough",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-7-RQ-07-RE]: Upstream vendor-supplied component hashes must be carried through into the SBOM"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CRA prEN 40000-1-3 [PRE-7-RQ-07-RE]: Upstream vendor-supplied component hashes must be carried through into the SBOM. References: CRA Annex I Part II; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07; prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07-RE."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\nWhere the fix goes:\n- CycloneDX: add components[].hashes[] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- SPDX 2.x: add packages[].checksums[] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- SPDX 3.0: add verifiedUsing[] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\nReferences:\n- CRA Annex I Part II (https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07-RE",
                "markdown": "Add cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or stronger) to components for integrity verification.\n\n**Where the fix goes**\n\n- **CycloneDX:** add components\\[\\].hashes\\[\\] entries with alg SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512 and the content.\n- **SPDX 2.x:** add packages\\[\\].checksums\\[\\] entries with algorithm SHA256, SHA384 or SHA512 and the checksumValue (PackageChecksum).\n- **SPDX 3.0:** add verifiedUsing\\[\\] Hash entries with algorithm sha256, sha384 or sha512 and the hashValue.\n\n**References**\n\n- [CRA Annex I Part II](<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng>)\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07\n- prEN 40000-1-3: PRE-7-RQ-07-RE"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
